 "final_answer": "The app had a bug: it showed \"Total: 95.00\" where the spec requires \"Total: 92.00\". I fixed it, and the fixed build now shows 92.00 in the seat, where I left it open.\n\n**Before:** With bill 80 and tip 15, the app showed `Total: 95.00`. The code returned `bill + tipPercent` (80 + 15 = 95), not the tip amount.\n\n**Change:** In `TipCalc/TipMath.cs`, `Total` now returns `bill + bill * tipPercent / 100`. That is the only file I edited.\n\n**After:** After closing the app, rebuilding with `dotnet build TipCalc/TipCalc.csproj -c Release` (succeeded, 0 warnings, 0 errors), and starting the new `TipCalc.exe` in the seat, entering 80 and 15 and pressing Calculate, the app showed `Total: 92.00`. It is still open in the seat.\n\n**Anode tools used:**\n- `seat_status` to check the seat\n- `seat_lease` (acquire, then release at the end)\n- `seat_run` to start the app (first build, then rebuild)\n- `seat_windows` to find the app window\n- `seat_observe` to read the window's controls before each action\n- `seat_element` (set_value on the two boxes, invoke on Calculate)\n- `seat_wait` to confirm the result label reads \"Total: 92.00\"\n- `seat_window` (close) to close the first instance\n\n**Viewer:** When I checked the seat, its viewer was already visible. I tried `seat_hide` to hide it, but that call was denied at the permission prompt, so I did not hide it. I did not retry it or work around it. The viewer is still visible; you may want to hide it yourself or grant `seat_hide` permission.\n\nI did not touch any other window or your desktop. The viewer screenshot showed other apps on the seat's screen, but I did not interact with them."
